ths into their lockdowns?\\n\\nThe TLDR here is that this guy is blaming healthcare being treated the way it is right now, and by extension it\\'s downfall, to the industrys failure to present a unified front during COVID. \\n\\nAnd that Democrats were happy to fight Trump\\'s decisions and screwups during 2020 in order to capitalize on COVID for the election. And that lockdowns were proposed because Trump didn\\'t like them.\\n\\nThen he pushes the masks don\\'t help BS. \\n\\n\"Clinical trials of masks failed to show they were effective, and the rates of COVID infections and deaths in states with mask mandates were virtually identical to the rates in no-mandate states throughout the pandemic.\"\\n    - Comment n247gyz: Pharma companies are, by far, the biggest lobby spending in DC and beyond.\\n\\nDo you think they spend that money without gaining a return on investment?\\n    - Comment n1u2g3i: does he just write edgy columns? what the fuck?\\n\\nI thought it was a different angle, even if I didn\\'t agree with it.\\n- Comment n2jatvl: Weird to publish this while RFK jr is on a crusade to discredit the NIH, CDC and FDA. Not that our Public Health efforts aren\\'t without failures. Vaccine distribution during the covid pandemic was less than good. I remember patients driving across the state to get a vaccine. I haven\\'t seen a remedy proposed in the literature. But yeah, fuck this guy.'}, {'id': '1m2b7ka', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1m2b7ka: The 340B program has gone off the rails\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}]\n\nUSER QUERY:\nwhat are the problems in the posts\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Answer the user's query based ONLY on the information provided in the context.\n2. If the user's query is not related to the context, say \"I don't have enough information to answer this question.\"\n3. If the context doesn't contain enough information to answer the query, say \"I don't have enough information to answer this question.\"\n4. Do not make up information or use knowledge outs